1
00:00:00,119 --> 00:00:03,159
OpenClaude 2.0 just dropped and it makes AI coding multiplayer.

2
00:00:06,159 --> 00:00:09,559
The open source agent Harness calls this its biggest release ever.

3
00:00:10,539 --> 00:00:14,119
933 contributors merged over 16,000 pull requests,

4
00:00:14,399 --> 00:00:16,819
roughly half of everything ever merged into the project.

5
00:00:17,340 --> 00:00:19,840
The headline feature, shared cloud sessions,

6
00:00:20,199 --> 00:00:22,119
so your whole team works inside one agent.

7
00:00:22,979 --> 00:00:27,839
Creator Peter Steinberger says local harnesses feel like relics of the past now.

8
00:00:28,180 --> 00:00:30,159
One catch before you roll it out at work,

9
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:34,419
reviewers note sandboxing and command approvals ship off by default.

10
00:00:34,719 --> 00:00:35,899
Lock those down first.

11
00:00:38,939 --> 00:00:41,919
So would you put your whole team inside one shared agent,

12
00:00:42,119 --> 00:00:46,259
or is one agent per developer the only sane way to work?

13
00:00:47,959 --> 00:00:54,699
